Z||000000||N_Man||04-16-2000||05:49 PM||||I know there have been a million and one questions about the pegging temp gauge. (I looked through most) But here is my question anyway<BR>My 87GT's temp gauge pegs at startup and then falls to where the ticks just start and might move to about the second or third tick at full operating temp.  past threads seem to indicate that fuel gauge is also related. my fuel gauge also reads inaccuratly, it reads full or almost for the first quarter tank and when it reads empty there is about a quater tank left.<BR>Im not so worried about my gauge pegging as i am its accuracy.  Any help is greatly appreciated. Thanks<p>[This message has been edited by N_Man (edited 04-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||daved||04-16-2000||08:19 PM||||N, Fiero Gauges are notoriously innacurate.  We all complain about them.  Most of us just live with it.  Your Temp. Gauge might (I say Might!) improve if you change the sensor ( by the distributor on a V6)||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||04-16-2000||09:16 PM||||The 2 problems are not related.<P>Fuel gauge problem is caused by the tank sendor and/or a bad tank ground.<P>Temp peg is a known problem in the Fiero wiring. There are 2 fixes. 1. is a full fix that corrects the GM wire error. 2. is a partial fix that only stops the thing pegging. 1. takes about an hour. 2. takes about 15-20 minutes max.<P>Temp gauge accuracy error is likely the sendor, a bad sendor ground, or the needle on the gauge has been knocked out of place.||||reg||1
